WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:05.200
December of 2019 is going to be a fateful
time for Netflix, with Disney+ having gone

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:06.799
live in the middle of November.

00:00:06.799 --> 00:00:10.780
Here are few titles jumping from to Disney
in December, plus a few more leaving Netflix

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:12.300
not owned by the House of Mouse.

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:16.740
If you haven't seen this particular Marvel
Cinematic Universe offering yet, now's as

00:00:16.741 --> 00:00:17.810
good a time as any.

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:21.820
The third installment of the Thor series is
one of the higher-rated and more widely acclaimed

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:24.009
installments in the entire MCU.

00:00:24.009 --> 00:00:28.090
Even those who typically don't get into superhero
films tend to make an exception for this one,

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:30.410
with its expert blend of action, heart, and
humor.

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:32.480
"Wanna use a big wooden fork?"

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:33.960
"No."

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.840
"Yeah, not really useful, unless you were
fighting off three vampires that were huddled

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:38.260
together."

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:43.600
As with all MCU films, it does help to have
seen a few others before diving into Ragnarok,

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:48.070
but the film is a fairly well-contained story
that outside context only enhances, rather

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:49.140
than being a necessity.

00:00:49.789 --> 00:00:54.380
Directed by Taika Waititi, Ragnarok sees the
God of Thunder learning some new and uncomfortable

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:57.720
hidden truths about Asgardian history and
his father, Odin.

00:00:58.109 --> 00:01:03.000
A conflict with a new and powerful enemy sends
Thor to the secret world of Sakaar, ruled

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.420
over by the Grandmaster, and home to his ruthless
gladiator games.

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:11.380
Along with old friends and new alliances,
Thor must survive and find a way to flee Sakaar

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:15.850
to save his homeland from the threat of Ragnarok,
the prophecy that foretells the destruction

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:17.680
of the entire Asgardian race.

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:20.640
Thor: Ragnarok will be leaving Netflix on
December 4th.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:26.820
With a box office take of $1.3 billion, there
aren't many sci-fi fans left who haven't seen

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.440
Star Wars: The Last Jedi at least once.

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:34.160
If you somehow missed it, this is probably
the last opportunity to stream it on a third-party

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:37.280
platform before it reemerges on Disney+ forevermore.

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:42.560
Writer/director Rian Johnson makes a concerted
effort to both enrich Star Wars lore, and

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:47.110
to play with expectations, giving fresh perspectives
of what we know about the Jedi and the universe

00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:48.520
in which Star Wars exists.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:50.920
"The Force is not a power you have.

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:56.220
It's not about lifting rocks, it's the energy
between all things."

00:01:56.720 --> 00:02:00.850
The Last Jedi immediately picks up where The
Force Awakens left off, with Rey beginning

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:03.020
a proper education in the use of the Force.

00:02:03.549 --> 00:02:07.960
In doing so, she'll discover many truths about
the Jedi, Luke Skywalker, and his relationship

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:08.700
with Kylo Ren.

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:13.030
Meanwhile, division begins to roil within
the Resistance, and the First Order is on

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:16.340
the hunt, hoping to destroy the Resistance's
high command at last.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:21.090
As Rey begins to realize that nothing is what
it seems, how will she go forward, both for

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:23.300
her own sake and that of the Resistance?

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:26.320
Star Wars: The Last Jedi leaves Netflix on
December 25th.

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:33.040
Seeing the 1982 feature The Dark Crystal before
it leaves Netflix is of particular importance

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:35.830
if you have watched, or want to get around
to watching, Netflix's revival series The

00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:37.580
Dark Crystal: Age of Resistance.

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:42.000
The modern series is set well before the events
of the film, and chronicles the downfall of

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:45.120
the world and near-extinction of the species
known as the Gelfling.

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:47.860
The movie may be going away, but not necessarily
forever.

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:52.680
Jim Henson's Muppet works and characters are
owned by Disney, but The Dark Crystal film

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:56.830
and its characters are owned entirely by The
Jim Henson Company, which is still an independent

00:02:56.830 --> 00:02:57.340
studio.

00:02:57.830 --> 00:03:01.800
The license will likely be re-upped at some
point in the future, especially if a second

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:03.520
season of the revival series is greenlit.

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:09.400
As for the film, The Dark Crystal, directed
by Jim Henson and Frank Oz, is a high-fantasy

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:13.170
story about the planet Thra, a world on the
edge of total destruction.

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:18.560
A thousand years before, the evil vulture-like
Skeksis shattered a magic crystal in order

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:21.000
to use it for themselves as a source of eternal
life.

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:24.940
Thra's last living Gelflings, Jen and Kira
[KEE-rah], undertake a quest to find the missing

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:29.709
shard and heal the crystal in hopes of destroying
the Skeksis and returning Thra to its former

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:31.300
thriving and lush green state.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:34.360
The Dark Crystal departs Netflix on December
31.

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:40.480
Schindler's List likely needs no introduction;
the 1993 historical drama appeared on Leonard

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:45.260
Maltin's list of the 100 most important films
of the 20th century and won a small avalanche

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:47.180
of awards, including six Oscars.

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:52.040
Directed by Steven Spielberg, the film is
an adaptation of the historical fiction novel

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:52.760
Schindler's Ark.

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:57.680
While it depicts actual events, and the central
characters did exist, some of the narrative

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:00.980
lacks firm historical record and has been
filled in with supposition.

00:04:01.690 --> 00:04:05.680
The film tells the story of Oskar Schindler,
a factory owner who saved over a thousand

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:09.720
Jewish people from death at the hands of the
Nazi regime by trafficking them through his

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:10.280
business.

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:14.820
Schindler begins as a faithful Nazi party
member enjoying status among the SS, employing

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:17.480
Jews recruited from the ghetto for cheap labor.

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:22.260
When the ghetto is purged, however, the violence
is so extreme that Schindler's allegiance

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:22.800
is forever altered.

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:28.520
Afterwards, he begins working with his Jewish
business partner in secret to secure the safety

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:29.580
of as many Jews as possible.

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:32.700
Schindler's List will leave Netflix on December
31.

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:38.380
Wet Hot American Summer, released in 2001
to underwhelming reviews and a brutal box

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:42.710
office, has developed a reputation as a nostalgic
cult classic in the years since.

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:47.740
Part of that is due to a talented cast that's
only gone on to huge success in the intervening

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:48.740
years since the film's release.

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:53.920
Among them are Christopher Meloni, David Hyde
Pierce, Janeane Garofalo, Paul Rudd, Amy Poehler,

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:54.880
and many more.

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:59.700
The film focuses on the last day of summer
camp at the fictional Camp Firewood in 1981,

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:04.820
where the various kids and camp counselors
fall in love, get into hijinks, and plan talent

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:05.360
shows...

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:06.560
"It sounds like pretty well-worn territory."

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:09.100
"The whole thing feels kinda trite.

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:09.780
I say we forget it."

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:11.480
"Is that how everyone feels?"

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:12.480
"Yeah."

00:05:13.510 --> 00:05:17.520
Well, they also try to save the camp from
being crushed by a piece of NASA's Skylab

00:05:17.530 --> 00:05:20.180
that happens to be plummeting through Earth's
atmosphere.

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:24.120
Wet Hot American Summer will also be departing
from Netflix on December 31.

